issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**
After updating the longitude and latitude of the document, the sorting result is still the result before the last update.
It is still invalid to delete and then add the document that needs to be updated.
The sorting will be correct only if all documents are deleted and then added.

**To Reproduce**
Steps to reproduce the behavior:
1. Writing Data  `[
	{
    "id": 1,
	"title":"自治县",
	"_geo": {
		"lat":30.891258,
		"lng": 104.520486
	},
	"address":"四川省绵阳市北川羌族自治1县"
  },
  	{
    "id": 2,
	"title":"顶锅山",
	"_geo": {
		"lat":30.311173,
		"lng": 104.745925
	},
	"address":"四川省成都市新都区"
  },
  	{
    "id": 3,
	"title":"集三路",
	"_geo": {
		"lat":30.891292,
		"lng": 104.485115
	},
	"address":"金堂县栖贤梨花沟风景区"
  },
  	{
    "id": 4,
	"title":"前进村",
	"_geo": {
		"lat":30.1517,
		"lng": 103.483306
	},
	"address":"四川省成都市蒲江县前进路"
  }
]`
2. Correct sorting when documents are not updated "_geoPoint(30.891292,104.435115):asc"   `{
			"id": 1,
			"title": "自治县",
			"_geo": {
				"lat": 30.891258,
				"lng": 104.520486
			},
			"address": "四川省绵阳市北川羌族自治1县",
			"_geoDistance": 8146,
			"_rankingScore": 1,
			"_rankingScoreDetails": {
				"_geoPoint(30.891292, 104.435115):asc": {
					"order": 0,
					"value": {
						"lat": 30.891258,
						"lng": 104.520486
					},
					"distance": 8146.2
				}
			}
		}`
3. When I update the data of document ID 1, the current document ranking will no longer be accurate. You can see that the last _geo  `{
			"id": 1,
			"title": "自治县",
			"_geo": {
				"lat": 31.891258,
				"lng": 104.520486
			},
			"address": "四川省绵阳市北川羌族自治1县",
			"_geoDistance": 111486,
			"_rankingScore": 1,
			"_rankingScoreDetails": {
				"_geoPoint(30.891292, 104.435115):asc": {
					"order": 0,
					"value": {
						"lat": 30.891258,
						"lng": 104.520486
					},
					"distance": 8146.2
				}
			}
		}`
4. See error

**Expected behavior**
After updating the document _geo, I hope the sorting can also be handled correctly

**Screenshots**

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a7538f4-3319-468d-8d50-c7eccff3013f)

**Meilisearch version:**
1.13.2

comments:
Hey @sliuxiangyin, I could reproduce your issue, thanks a lot for the report it’s definitely a bug.
Here’s a simpler reproducer:

1. make the geo field sortable
2. Add three documents all aligned on the same latitude: `[{ "id": 1, "_geo": {"lat":0,"lng":0} }, { "id": 2, "_geo": {"lat":1,"lng":0} }, { "id": 3, "_geo": {"lat":2,"lng":0} }]`
3. Make a search sorting by `geoPoint`: `{ "sort": ["_geoPoint(10,0):asc"]}` => it works
4. Update one document: `{ "id": 1, "_geo": {"lat":3,"lng":0} }`
5. Make the same search requests => BUG, the documents are not returned in the expected order
```json
{
  "hits": [
    {
      "id": 3,
      "_geo": {
        "lat": 2,
        "lng": 0
      },
      "_geoDistance": 889559
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "_geo": {
        "lat": 1,
        "lng": 0
      },
      "_geoDistance": 1000754
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "_geo": {
        "lat": 3,
        "lng": 0
      },
      "_geoDistance": 778364
    }
  ],
  "query": "",
  "processingTimeMs": 1,
  "limit": 20,
  "offset": 0,
  "estimatedTotalHits": 3
}
```
